      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "A point $(2, 5)$ is rotated $180°$ about the origin. What are the coordinates of the image?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$(5, 2)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$(-2, -5)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$(-5, -2)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$(2, -5)$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "A $180°$ rotation about the origin maps $(x, y) \\to (-x, -y)$. So $(2, 5) \\to (-2, -5)$."
